<!-- .slide: style="text-align: center" -->
# CMake is NOT Make
or how to forget about the build system

<small>M2 Internals Meeting,<br />May 8th, 2020</small>


<!-- slide -->

### What is CMake?

<!-- pause -->

Make is a build system.
- configure <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
- make <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->

<!-- pause -->

CMake is a *meta*-build system.
- Does your job for you <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
- Generate build files for Ninja <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
- Integrate with IDEs like Xcode, VSCode, etc. <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
- Cross-platform <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
- Faster <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->

<!-- slide -->

![](https://media.giphy.com/media/12dsAPOI1YykFO/giphy.gif)

<!-- slide -->

### Download CMake
- `brew install cmake`
- `apt`, `dnf`, `pacman`, ...
- https://cmake.org/download/

<!-- pause -->

In a terminal, confirm that version is at least 3.15:
```bash
$ cmake --version
cmake version 3.17.1

```

<!-- slide -->

### Download Ninja

![](https://media.giphy.com/media/8bYrnHt3Ht7rV1nNCU/giphy.gif)

- On Debian/Ubuntu, install:
  - `ninja-build`.
- On Mac OS X, using Homebrew, install:
  - `ninja`.

<!-- slide -->

### Install library build tools
- On Debian/Ubuntu, install:
  - `autoconf build-essential bison libtool pkg-config yasm`.
- On Mac OS X, using Homebrew, install:
  - `autoconf automake bison libtool pkg-config yasm`.

<!-- slide -->

### Install required Macaulay2 libraries
- On Debian/Ubuntu, install:
  - `libopenblas-dev libeigen3-dev libxml2-dev libreadline-dev libomp-dev libtbb-dev libgdbm-dev libboost-stacktrace-dev libatomic-ops-dev`.
- On Mac OS X, using Homebrew, install:
  - `eigen libxml2 readline libomp tbb gdbm boost libatomic_ops`.

<!-- slide -->

#### Add and fetch new *remote*
```
$ git remote add mahrud https://github.com/mahrud/M2.git
$ git fetch mahrud
```
#### Checkout the branch
```
$ git checkout feature/cmake
```

<!-- slide -->

2. Setup the build environment:
```bash
$ cd M2/M2/BUILD/build
$ cmake -GNinja -S../.. -B. \
       -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr \
       -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
```

- build system generator <!-- .element: class="fragment" --> `-GNinja`
- source directory <!-- .element: class="fragment" --> `-S../..`
- build directory <!-- .element: class="fragment" --> `-B.`

<!-- pause -->

`-DNAME=VALUE` sets variable `NAME` to `VALUE`.
- install prefix <!-- .element: class="fragment" --> `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr`

<!-- pause -->

- `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE` determines various compiler flags to be used.
- `Debug`
- `Release`
- `RelMinSize`
- `RelWithDebInfo` (default)

<!-- slide -->

### Build the libraries
```
make build-libraries
```
```
ninja build-libraries
```

Important:  <!-- .element: class="fragment" -->
 his target **must** be built independently, before proceeding.

<!-- pause -->

You can force building certain libraries:
```
cmake -DBUILD_LIBRARIES="BDWGC;MPIR" .
```
Or to build everything:
```
cmake -DBUILD_LIBRARIES=ALL .
```

<!-- slide -->

### Build Macaulay2 binary and core
```
ninja M2-binary M2-core
```
The `M2-binary` is a prerequisite of `M2-core`, which is currently the default target, so just `ninja` also suffices.

<!-- slide -->

### Build the external programs
```
ninja build-programs
```

Similar to the libraries, `cmake -DBUILD_PROGRAMS=...` can be used to enforce building specific programs.

<!-- slide -->

### Install packages and generate documentation
```
ninja install-packages
```

<!-- slide -->

### Testing Macaulay2
There are unit-tests available within the `Macaulay2/e/unit-tests` and `Macaulay2/tests` directories which can be tested using the CTest utility.

<!-- pause -->

Here are various ways of using `ctest`:
- `ctest --build-and-test`
- `ctest -N`
- `ctest -R unit-tests`
- `ctest -R normal -j6`
- `ctest --rerun-failed -V`
- `ctest -R check-LocalRings -j4`
- `ctest -R check-LocalRings-2 -V`

Note: if the last option does not work, try running `ninja info-packages` and `cmake .` to populate the tests.

<!-- slide -->

### Installing Macaulay2
```
ninja install
```
```
cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr/local .
```
```
DESTDIR=/home/mahrud/staging ninja install
```

<!-- slide -->

### Packaging Macaulay2
```
cpack -G DEB	# requires dpkg
cpack -G RPM	# requires rpmbuild
```

<!-- slide -->

### Targets for Installing Macaulay2 Packages
The following targets involve the Macaulay2 packages located in the `Macaulay2/packages` subdirectory in the source:
- `list-packages`
- `install-packages`
- `check-packages`
- `uninstall-packages`

<!-- pause -->

For specific packages, the following targets are also available:
- `install-[PACKAGE]`
- `check-[PACKAGE]`
- `all-[PACKAGE]`
- `uninstall-[PACKAGE]`

<!-- slide -->

A quick build involves the following steps:
```
git clone https://github.com/mahrud/M2.git -b feature/cmake
cmake -GNinja -S M2/M2 -B M2/M2/BUILD/build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr
cmake --build M2/M2/BUILD/build --target build-libraries build-programs
cmake --build M2/M2/BUILD/build --target install-packages
cmake --build M2/M2/BUILD/build --target M2-emacs
cmake --install M2/M2/BUILD/build
```
